  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Bhutan is known worldwide for using renewable natural resources to produce electricity. Name at least three renewable resources used in Bhutan and briefly explain the principle of each type of power plant. (3 marks)', '1. Hydropower - Bhutan''s main source (Chukha, Tala, Kurichhu, Dagachhu, Mangdechhu, Punatsangchhu). Water from a river is stored or diverted and falls through penstocks; its potential energy becomes kinetic energy that spins a turbine connected to a generator, where electromagnetic induction produces electricity.
2. Solar power - photovoltaic (PV) panels on roofs and the solar plant at Sephu (Wangdue) convert sunlight directly into direct current electricity using semiconductor cells; an inverter converts it to AC.
3. Wind power - wind turbines at Rubesa (Wangdue): moving air turns the blades, which drive a generator.
(Biogas plants, in which animal dung is digested anaerobically to produce methane for cooking, are also used in rural Bhutan.)', null, '[{"point": "Hydropower (main source, e.g. Chukha, Tala, Punatsangchhu, Mangdechhu): potential energy of water stored/falling from a height turns a turbine coupled to a generator (electromagnetic induction)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Solar power (e.g. Sephu solar plant, rooftop panels): photovoltaic cells convert sunlight directly into electricity (photoelectric effect)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Wind power (e.g. Rubesa wind farm, Wangdue): moving air turns the blades of a wind turbine that drives a generator; (biogas/biomass also accepted)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
