  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'In February 2016, the Prime Minister of Bhutan said in a speech abroad: "This country isn''t just carbon neutral, it is carbon negative."

a) Explain why Bhutan is not only carbon neutral but also carbon negative. (1.5 marks)', 'a) Carbon neutral means a country''s emissions equal what it absorbs; carbon negative means it absorbs more than it emits. Bhutan''s forests cover over 70% of the land and absorb several times more carbon dioxide than the country produces from transport, industry and households. In addition, Bhutan exports clean hydroelectricity to India, which replaces electricity from fossil fuels and avoids further emissions.', null, '[{"point": "Bhutan''s forests (over 70% cover) absorb more CO₂ (about 6-9 million tonnes a year) than the country emits (about 2-3 million tonnes), so net emissions are negative", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Its exports of clean hydropower to India replace coal-fired electricity, offsetting further emissions", "marks": 0.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
