  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Copy the diagram of the heart and indicate with arrows the direction of the flow of blood in and out of the heart. Name the valves present in the human heart, with their location. (3 marks)', 'Direction of flow (arrows on the diagram): deoxygenated blood enters the right atrium from the superior and inferior venae cavae → passes through the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle → is pumped through the pulmonary valve into the pulmonary artery to the lungs. Oxygenated blood returns through the four pulmonary veins into the left atrium → passes through the mitral (bicuspid) valve into the left ventricle → is pumped through the aortic valve into the aorta and to the whole body.
Valves:
• Tricuspid valve - between the right atrium and right ventricle.
• Mitral (bicuspid) valve - between the left atrium and left ventricle.
• Pulmonary (semilunar) valve - at the exit of the right ventricle into the pulmonary artery.
• Aortic (semilunar) valve - at the exit of the left ventricle into the aorta.', null, '[{"point": "Flow: venae cavae → right atrium → right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs → pulmonary veins → left atrium → left ventricle → aorta → body", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Atrioventricular valves: tricuspid (between right atrium and right ventricle) and bicuspid/mitral (between left atrium and left ventricle)", "marks": 0.75}, {"point": "Semilunar valves: pulmonary valve (at the opening of the pulmonary artery from the right ventricle) and aortic valve (at the opening of the aorta from the left ventricle)", "marks": 0.75}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
