  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Explain what you understand from the two graphs about the catalytic action of enzymes (energy profile with and without enzyme; initial velocity against substrate concentration). Explain Vmax and Km, and write some important characteristics of a catalyst. (3 marks)', 'Graph 1 (energy profile): with an enzyme the energy hill between reactants and products is lower - the enzyme lowers the activation energy by providing an alternative pathway, so more molecules can react and the reaction is faster. The overall energy released by the reaction (difference between reactants and products) is the same with or without the enzyme.
Graph 2 (Michaelis-Menten curve): at low substrate concentration the initial velocity rises almost in proportion to the substrate; at high concentration it levels off because all active sites are occupied.
• Vmax - the maximum rate reached when the enzyme is saturated with substrate.
• Km (Michaelis constant) - the substrate concentration at which the rate is half of Vmax; a low Km means the enzyme has a high affinity for its substrate.
Characteristics of a catalyst: it is chemically unchanged at the end; a small amount is enough; it does not change the position of equilibrium or ΔH; it speeds up forward and reverse reactions equally; it cannot start a reaction that is not feasible; enzymes are highly specific and work best at an optimum temperature and pH.', null, '[{"point": "Graph 1: the enzyme lowers the activation energy (lower peak) so the reaction is faster; the overall energy released (reactants to products) is unchanged", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Graph 2: rate rises with substrate concentration then levels off; Vmax = maximum rate when all enzyme active sites are saturated; Km = substrate concentration at half Vmax (low Km = high affinity)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Catalyst characteristics: unchanged at the end, needed in small amounts, does not change equilibrium or ΔH, speeds forward and reverse reactions equally, specific (enzymes) and affected by temperature/pH", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
