  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Hand hygiene is the most important measure to prevent hospital-acquired infections. State the WHO ''five moments for hand hygiene'' and the correct method of hand rubbing. (3 marks)', 'WHO five moments for hand hygiene:
1. Before touching a patient.
2. Before a clean or aseptic procedure (e.g. inserting a catheter, giving an injection).
3. After a body-fluid exposure risk (blood, urine, secretions, removing gloves).
4. After touching a patient.
5. After touching the patient''s surroundings (bed, equipment), even if the patient was not touched.
Method: use an alcohol-based hand rub for 20-30 seconds, or soap and running water for 40-60 seconds when hands are visibly dirty or after caring for patients with diarrhoea. Remove rings and watches; rub palm to palm, the back of each hand, between the fingers, the backs of the fingers, each thumb (rotational rubbing) and the fingertips in the palms; rinse and dry with a single-use towel, turning off the tap with the towel.', null, '[{"point": "Five moments (1): before touching a patient; before a clean/aseptic procedure; after body-fluid exposure risk", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Five moments (2): after touching a patient; after touching patient surroundings", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Method: alcohol rub 20-30 s (or soap and water 40-60 s) covering palms, backs, between fingers, backs of fingers, thumbs, fingertips; remove jewellery, dry hands, use soap and water when visibly soiled", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
